# Parcego Super Admin Dashboard – Cursor Rule

## Objective

Build the Super Admin Dashboard UI for the Parcego Courier Business Platform, strictly following the provided user flowchart and naming/scoping conventions.  
**No backend logic or API integration—focus is on layout, navigation, and user experience.**

---

## 1. Technology & Design System

- **Framework:** Next.js 14+ (App Router)
- **Language:** TypeScript
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS only
- **UI Components:** shadcn/ui (https://ui.shadcn.com/)
- **State Management:** Zustand (for client-side state, if needed)
- **Transitions:** Use premium, subtle transitions as per `@premium-transitions-and-effects.mdc`
- **Accessibility:** All UI must be accessible (ARIA, keyboard navigation, color contrast)
- **Naming/Scoping:** All IDs and class names must follow `@naming-and-scoping.mdc`:
  - IDs: `parcego-[component]-[purpose]-[unique-identifier]`
  - Classes: `parcego-[block]__[element]--[modifier]`

---

## 2. Scope & Requirements

### Super Admin Dashboard Features (All UI, No Backend)
- **Platform Overview:** System health, total shipments, active users, revenue, etc. (summary cards)
- **Manage Merchants:** List/table of merchants (mock data), with actions (view, approve, suspend, edit)
- **Manage Couriers:** List/table of couriers (mock data), with actions (onboard, verify, deactivate)
- **Platform Analytics:** Charts and trends (mock data)
- **Operational Management:** Platform settings, notifications, and controls (UI only)
- **Recent Activity Feed:** Log of recent platform events (mock)
- **Navigation:** Sidebar or top nav for dashboard sections (Overview, Merchants, Couriers, Analytics, Settings)
- **Profile/Account Menu:** Avatar with dropdown for account settings and logout (UI only)
- **Mobile-First:** Fully responsive, mobile-optimized layout

---

## 3. Navigation

- Use Next.js App Router for all navigation.
- All flows must match the provided user flowchart.
- All navigation and state changes handled client-side (no server calls).

---

## 4. Data & Logic

- All data is static, mocked, or placeholder.
- No API calls, no backend logic, no authentication.
- Use mock data for lists, charts, and status updates.

---

## 5. Code Quality & Structure

- Use TypeScript everywhere.
- Functional components only.
- Early returns, no dead code, no TODOs.
- Descriptive naming and clear structure.
- All forms, buttons, and flows must be visually complete and accessible.
- All IDs and class names must strictly follow `@naming-and-scoping.mdc`.

---

## 6. Deliverables

- Super Admin Dashboard page and all required UI components.
- Fully navigable UI demo (no backend).
- README update with instructions for running the frontend demo.

---

## 7. Enforcement

- Code reviews must verify adherence to this rule file and referenced standards.
- Any deviation must be documented and approved by the project lead.

---

**Goal:**  
Deliver a pixel-perfect, accessible, and modern Super Admin Dashboard UI, ready for future backend/API integration.

